Subject: [PATCH] guild chat skips filler and invented reputation claims

WHY THIS PATCH EXISTS

BroadcastHelper (src/Util/BroadcastHelper.cpp at the pin below) sends
every template broadcast to a per-broadcast list of channels. Four of
its broadcasts are not about anything the speaker did, and all four
could land in the guild channel:

  - BroadcastSuggestSomething, BroadcastSuggestSomethingToxic and
    BroadcastSuggestToxicLinks pick a random row from the
    suggest_something (134 rows), suggest_something_toxic (102) and
    suggest_toxic_links text classes - ambient filler - and listed
    {TO_GUILD, 10} first. One suggest_something row is "%my_role is
    looking for guild." (text id 741), so a bot that is already in a
    guild advertised for one in its own guild channel, with %my_role
    expanding through ChatHelper::FormatClass to the premade spec
    link, which arrived as fragmented colour spans.
  - BroadcastSuggestGrindReputation chooses %faction at random from a
    list and %rep_level at random from three levels; neither is read
    from the speaker's actual standings. Its suggest_faction lines
    ("Need just a bit to be %rep_level with %faction.") are claims
    about a grind the speaker may not have, and its list carried
    {TO_GUILD, 50}.

Measured in the relayed guild feed over one evening in October 2026:
modern-slang filler, the broken recruitment line, and reputation
boasts for factions the speakers had no standing with made up most of
what a reader saw. Full trace: the guild-chat realism ticket in the
companion website/bridge tracker.

This patch removes the guild entry from those four broadcasts and
changes nothing else. Broadcasts grounded in the speaker's own
activity (loot, quest accepted/progress/turn-in, kills, level-ups)
and genuine asks (suggest_instance, suggest_quest, suggest_trade for
grind materials) keep their guild entry - a guild hearing what its
members did and what they need is the point of the channel. The
filler keeps its world and general entries; only the toxic classes
also default to chance 0 in the shipped conf, and this patch does not
change that.

WHAT WOULD LET THIS PATCH BE DELETED

Upstream (or the operator's fork, which is where this tree comes
from) doing any one of: gating the suggest broadcasts on the
speaker's guild membership and actual standings, dropping the guild
entry from these four channel lists, or adding a per-speaker guild
broadcast cooldown that makes the filler rare enough to read as a
person rather than a rotation.

APPLIES TO

mod-playerbots @ 40884e9c135c1daf27ffd894a6047502a5701130 (the
deployment pin read 2026-10-28), on top of local patches 0001-0016.
Touches only the channel lists of BroadcastSuggestGrindReputation,
BroadcastSuggestSomething, BroadcastSuggestSomethingToxic and
BroadcastSuggestToxicLinks in src/Util/BroadcastHelper.cpp.

